ELK Setup\ulnone\fs36\par
\fs28 1. Download Elastic search and extract in some folder e.g "elasticsearch-8.7.1".\par
2. Start elasticsearch \par
\fs22 elasticsearch-8.7.1\\bin>elasticsearch.bat\fs28       \par
3. Add a new user for Kibana and logstash by using command like below : \par
\fs22 E:\\Abdul\\Microservices\\ELK\\elasticsearch-8.7.1-windows-x86_64\\elasticsearch-8.7.1\\bin>elasticsearch-users useradd -r superuser abdul\par
pass for this test setup : mohsin\fs28\par
4.  Note down the token from the elastic search logs , it will be used in the Kibana setup\par
5. Download Kibana and start it using below : \par
  /bin/kibana\par
6. Open Kibana console ( e.g {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK http://localhost:5601/ }}{\fldrslt{http://localhost:5601/\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs28 ) and setup using the elastic search token\par

