7. Now download and setup logstash which can read all logs from a centralized location and feed it to Elastic search \par
8.  Update sample config file : logstash-sample.conf like below to take logs input from some centralized location , extract Key-value metrics from each log and push it to the elastic server.\par

\pard\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\fs14 input \{\par
  file \{\par
    type => "log"\par
    path => "E:/Abdul/Microservices/logs/*.log" \par
    start_position => beginning\tab\par
  \}\par
\}\par
filter \{\par
 grok \{\par
    match => [ "message",\par
               "%\{TIMESTAMP_ISO8601:timestamp1\}  %\{WORD:loglevel\} \\[%\{GREEDYDATA:appname\},%\{GREEDYDATA:traceId\},%\{GREEDYDATA:spanid\}\\] %\{NUMBER:processID\} %\{GREEDYDATA:out\}"               \par
             ]\par
  \}\par
  date \{\par
    match => [ "timestamp" , "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSS" ]\par
  \}\par
\}\par
output \{\par
  elasticsearch \{\par
    hosts => ["{{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK https://localhost:9200 }}{\fldrslt{https://localhost:9200\ul0\cf0}}}}\f0\fs14 "]\par
\tab cacert \highlight2 => 'config/cert/http_ca.crt'\par
\highlight0\tab user => logstash_internal\par
    password => abdul1234\par
\tab index =>"ecommerce"\par
  \}\par
 \}\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\fs28 9.  Pls note the communication with elastic search is through HTTPS , the cacert configured above is the self signed certificate copied from the elastic server path ( e.g elasticsearch-8.7.1\\config\\certs\\http_ca.crt)\par
10. Create the user configured above (e.g logstash_internal) in Kibana with proper roles :\par
